{"kind": "tool_approval", "tool": "book_chapter_save_draft", "args": {"body": "The air in the archives was thick with the scent of ancient parchment and the metallic tang of dying embers. Elara traced the gilded runes of the Ember Codex, her fingers trembling. It wasn't just the heat radiating from the leather binding that unsettled her, but the way the light seemed to dance within the ink itself, as if the words were breathing.

"It's waking up," she whispered, the sound swallowed by the vast, silent halls of the Great Library.

Outside, the sky was a bruised purple, torn by the first streaks of a crimson dawn. The prophecy had spoken of a fire that would not consume, but rewrite. As the first rune on the cover pulsed with a dull, rhythmic glow, Elara realized the Codex wasn't just a book of history—it was a countdown.", "book_id": "01a05944-0d01-7a2c-b151-4697218cd67b", "chapter": "1", "chapter_id": "01a05944-0d9b-7253-aace-d530b779a037"}, "tier": "A"}

