{"kind": "tool_approval", "tool": "book_chapter_save_draft", "args": {"body": "The air in the archives was thick with the scent of old parchment and something sharper, like the ozone before a lightning strike. Elara traced the embossed lettering on the spine of the heavy, leather-bound volume. It was the Ember Codex, a relic whispered about in the lower districts but rarely seen by anyone with a legitimate title.

As her fingers brushed the cover, a faint warmth pulsed against her skin. The runes etched into the leather glowed with a dull, dying ember-light, as if the book itself were breathing. She knew the risks of opening it—the stories of scholars lost to the madness of the flame—but the secrets held within were the only way to save the city before the frost took everything.

She pulled the book from the shelf, the silence of the library suddenly feeling heavy, expectant. The Ember Codex was awake.", "book_id": "01a05947-6c3c-73e0-a699-cd82e30717e0", "chapter": "Chapter I — The Ember Codex", "chapter_id": "01a05947-6ce5-71c2-a020-cbfa8562e1b3"}, "tier": "A"}

